        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e6293a00-7fd4-561b-8519-3a3fc142e4bf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anna Kournikova, Martina Hingis, Jana Novotná, Natasha Zvereva, Lindsay Davenport, Mary Pierce, Serena Williams, Venus Williams, Bob Harper, Dolvett Quince\n- Events: 1999 French Open – Women's Doubles, The Biggest Loser (season 12)\n- Roles: tennis players, trainers\n\nFacts:\n- Anna Sergeyevna Kournikova was born on 7 June 1981 and is a Russian former professional tennis player.\n- At the 1999 French Open – Women's Doubles, Jana Novotná partnered with Natasha Zvereva as the first seed, and Martina Hingis partnered with Anna Kournikova as the second seed.\n- At the 1999 French Open – Women's Doubles, Novotná and Zvereva retired in their quarterfinal match against Lindsay Davenport and Mary Pierce.\n- At the 1999 French Open – Women's Doubles, Hingis and Kournikova reached the final but lost to Serena and Venus Williams 6–3, 6–7, 8–6.\n- In The Biggest Loser season 12, Anna Kournikova and Dolvett Quince joined existing trainer Bob Harper as new trainers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
